@startuml
package SharedLogicCore {

    ' === Abstract base classes ===
    abstract class UserProfile {
        +_id : Guid
        +ComputeHash() : int
    }

    ' === Interfaces ===
    interface ICommandData

    ' === Data Transfer Object ===
    class ExecuteCommandRequestDTO {
        +CommandType : string
        +CommandData : object
        +StateHash : int
    }

    ' === Core command processor ===
    abstract class GameCommandProcessor {
        -_handlers : Dictionary<Type, CommandHandler>
        +CreateDefaultProfile(Guid userId) : UserProfile
        +ExecuteCommand(UserProfile profile, ICommandData command) : void        
        #RegisterHandler<TProfile, TCommand>(handler) : void
    }

    ' === Dependencies / Relationships ===
    UserProfile <.. GameCommandProcessor : uses
    ICommandData <.. GameCommandProcessor : uses
    ICommandData <|.. ExecuteCommandRequestDTO : contains
}

note top of ICommandData
Implemented in each game plugin for every possible
user action.
end note

note bottom of GameCommandProcessor
    The central engine for registering and executing game commands.
    Extended for each game (e.g., ConnectFourCommandProcessor).
end note

note top of UserProfile
    Abstract user profile, extended in each game plugin.
end note

note bottom of ExecuteCommandRequestDTO
Used to send a message from client to server.
In order to correct deserialization we need field CommandType.
StateHash we use to ensure that UserProfile is in the same state
after executing command on client and server. 
end note

@enduml
